WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.164
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 2. Topic: Laws of Indices. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:10.584 --> 00:00:19.618
Simplify (uv squared) to the power 5 over u to the power 7 v to the power minus 3 and express your answer with positive indices.

3
00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:23.351
STEP 1.

4
00:00:23.511 --> 00:00:35.904
Key rule: Power of a Product & Power of a Power. (ab) to the power n equals a to the power n b to the power n, (a to the power m) to the power n equals a to the power mn.

5
00:00:36.064 --> 00:00:40.134
Apply the outer index to every factor inside the bracket.

6
00:00:40.294 --> 00:00:51.309
Apply the power-of-a-product law (ab) to the power n equals a to the power n b to the power n and the power-of-a-power law (a to the power m) to the power n equals a to.

7
00:00:51.469 --> 00:01:01.530
the power mn: (uv squared) to the power 5 equals u to the power 5 (v squared) to the power 5 equals u to the power 5 v to the power 10.

8
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.451
STEP 2.

9
00:01:05.611 --> 00:01:14.832
Key rule: Quotient Law of Indices. a to the power m over a to the power n equals a to the power m-n (a is not equal to 0).

10
00:01:14.992 --> 00:01:19.179
Subtract the index of the denominator from that of the numerator.

11
00:01:19.339 --> 00:01:25.426
Divide using a to the power m over a to the power n equals a to the power m-n for each base.

12
00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:36.908
u to the power 5 v to the power 10 over u to the power 7 v to the power minus 3 equals u to the power 5 minus 7 v to the power 10 minus (minus 3) equals u to the power.

13
00:01:37.068 --> 00:01:40.289
minus 2 v to the power 13.

14
00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:44.328
STEP 3.

15
00:01:44.488 --> 00:01:54.982
Key rule: Negative Index Law. a to the power minus n equals 1 over a to the power n. Turn every negative index into a positive one by flipping the base.

16
00:01:55.142 --> 00:02:02.255
Rewrite the negative index as a positive one, since a to the power minus n equals 1 over a to the power n.

17
00:02:02.415 --> 00:02:08.643
u to the power minus 2 v to the power 13 equals v to the power 13 over u squared.

18
00:02:09.063 --> 00:02:13.616
So the answer is: v to the power 13 over u squared.

19
00:02:14.036 --> 00:02:22.844
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 2. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
